***Customer logic :- 

1. makeCustomerDataSet() :- 
- this creates a table the stores the data of customers and the money that each customer had spend 
- it makes only three columns , NO, Name , Money spend
- if a customer name is more than 16 character, the table will be disrupted 
- the distance between each number in the column of indecies in the file is 63 byte 
- the distance betwen each '|' in the customer name blank is 16 , the positions of the first pair of ‘|’ is in (38, 54) and the 
positions of '|'  pairs in row x are in positions (38 + x * 63 , 54 +  x * 63). 
- the distance between each consecutive characters within rows is 63, for example the distance between 1 and 2 is 63  

2. jumpAddName() deleteName() :- 
- this function is designed specifically for customer.txt file
- given the index of the customer, it add his name in the proper box
- if given a name that it's length is more than 16, it will disrupt the customer.txt

3. drawMenu() :- 
- this function take the inventory.txt and prints only the departments the customer is interested in to the terminal 
- draw to the customer in the screen the names and prices of items
- it jump into inventory.txt and abstracts the names and prices only 
- because the customer is only interested in knowing the names and prices 


4. getItemData()  :- 
- this function jump into the inventory.txt and grap the price, name, quantity and return it back 
- because no function can return more than on input at once , it is defined with parameters of type pointer and
takes addresses within the logic 
- it is designed specifically for inventory.txt



*** Storage logic :- 

1. makeInventory() :- 

- creates the inventory.txt 
- right now it just make a primitive inventory.txt to pass college exam but in the future it will be more dynamic and complex
- our supermarket departments are : Beverages , Meat, Fruit, Vegetables, Bakery, Dairy, Snacks 
- Names of items are not allowed to be more than 16 
- Amounts and Prices are not allowed to be values with more than 7 digits
- in this inventory.txt , the first occurrence of name = byte 172
- first occurrence of price = byte 188
- first occurrence of amount = byte 196
- first occurence of NO = byte 167
- width of each line = 51 byte 
- distance between each first and second name, first and second amount , first and second price = 102 byte

